Give the JSCOnly-on-iOS build a working JIT memory model.

Measured on the A10 (iPad7,12, 17.6.1, bare-fakesigned) with the probes in
linux-build/probes-bun-jit/:

  * MAP_JIT is refused outright (EINVAL).
  * An RWX anonymous mapping is created happily and then SIGBUSes on the first
    instruction fetch, so JSC's "write straight through the RWX pool" path is
    dead.
  * mach_vm_remap gives a second RW view of the pool, and writes through it are
    executed by the RX view -- ENABLE(SEPARATED_WX_HEAP), which this WebKit
    still carries in full.
  * But only for a page that is already resident in the executable mapping.
    iOS will not fault a dirty anonymous page into a fresh executable mapping;
    it will re-protect a page that already has an entry. So each page has to be
    faulted in through the exec mapping as RW and flipped to RX once, after
    which alias writes are honoured for the life of the process.

That last point is the whole shape of this patch: the pool is committed page by
page anyway, so the flip rides along in OSAllocator::commit(), and the exec
view's *maximum* protection has to stay RWX for that flip to be permitted.

The commit() hook must not disturb the contents of the range it flips. The
first version of this zeroed each committed page, which is fine single-threaded
and deadlocks opencode within seconds once concurrent DFG is in play: the
compiler thread writes code through the alias into a region while another
thread commits a range covering it, and the memset erases code that is about to
be executed. It touches each page read-modify-write instead. That failure only
appears with DFG and concurrent JIT both on -- BUN_JSC_useDFGJIT=0 and
BUN_JSC_useConcurrentJIT=0 each hide it, which is what identified it.

USE(EXECUTE_ONLY_JIT_WRITE_FUNCTION) stays off: it protects the write thunk
with vm_protect(VM_PROT_EXECUTE) under a RELEASE_ASSERT and the A10 has no
execute-only memory. With it off JSC writes through genericWriteToJITRegion,
a plain memcpy into the writable alias.

Two smaller things this config trips over, both unrelated to memory:
memset_s is C11 Annex K and the iOS SDK only declares it under
__STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT1__, and ScriptExecutable.cpp's setupJIT() needs
CompilationResult complete when nothing else in its unified source pulls the
definition in (CodeBlock.h only forward-declares it).

mach_vm_remap is declared by wtf/spi/cocoa/MachVMSPI.h for non-MAC platforms,
so it needs no local declaration even though the iOS SDK's mach/mach_vm.h
omits it.
diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/ExecutableAllocator.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/ExecutableAllocator.cpp
index 75fe31a7754..4eece369453 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/ExecutableAllocator.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/jit/ExecutableAllocator.cpp
@@ -319,7 +319,16 @@ static ALWAYS_INLINE void initializeSeparatedWXHeaps(void* stubBase, size_t stub
 #endif
 
     // Prevent writing into the executable JIT mapping.
+#if OS(IOS_FAMILY)
+    // Current protection only. OSAllocator::commit() has to flip each page to
+    // RW to fault it in through this mapping before anything can execute out of
+    // it, which the kernel refuses once the maximum protection drops
+    // VM_PROT_WRITE. The steady state is unchanged: the current protection is
+    // RX and every write goes through the alias.
+    result = vm_protect(mach_task_self(), reinterpret_cast<vm_address_t>(jitBase), jitSize, false, VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_EXECUTE);
+#else
     result = vm_protect(mach_task_self(), reinterpret_cast<vm_address_t>(jitBase), jitSize, true, VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_EXECUTE);
+#endif
     RELEASE_ASSERT(!result);
 
     // Prevent execution in the writable JIT mapping.
@@ -328,7 +337,17 @@ static ALWAYS_INLINE void initializeSeparatedWXHeaps(void* stubBase, size_t stub
 
 WTF_ALLOW_UNSAFE_BUFFER_USAGE_BEGIN
     // Zero out writableAddr to avoid leaking the address of the writable mapping.
+#if OS(IOS_FAMILY)
+    // memset_s is C11 Annex K, and the iOS SDK only declares it under
+    // __STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT1__ -- which a unified-source build cannot set late
+    // enough to matter. writableAddr is a stack local about to go out of scope,
+    // so a plain store plus a barrier the optimiser may not drop is equivalent
+    // here.
+    memset(&writableAddr, 0, sizeof(writableAddr));
+    asm volatile("" ::: "memory");
+#else
     memset_s(&writableAddr, sizeof(writableAddr), 0, sizeof(writableAddr));
+#endif
 WTF_ALLOW_UNSAFE_BUFFER_USAGE_END
 
 #if ENABLE(SEPARATED_WX_HEAP)
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
index b62d0feda92..46a3529c227 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformEnable.h
@@ -532,6 +532,13 @@
 #endif
 #endif
 
+/* iOS cannot execute a page that is currently writable, so the JIT region has
+   to be written through a separate RW mapping. PlatformEnableCocoa.h would
+   have set this, but it is only included for PLATFORM(COCOA). */
+#if !defined(ENABLE_SEPARATED_WX_HEAP) && OS(IOS_FAMILY) && CPU(ARM64)
+#define ENABLE_SEPARATED_WX_HEAP 1
+#endif
+
 #if !defined(ENABLE_SEPARATED_WX_HEAP)
 #define ENABLE_SEPARATED_WX_HEAP 0
 #endif
diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformHave.h b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformHave.h
index 9c53f471873..f7398f63e0f 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformHave.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/PlatformHave.h
@@ -84,6 +84,12 @@
 #define HAVE_REMAP_JIT 1
 #endif
 
+/* JSCOnly deliberately defines no PLATFORM(), so PLATFORM(COCOA) misses the
+   iOS port even though mach_vm_remap is exactly what its JIT needs. */
+#if !defined(HAVE_REMAP_JIT) && OS(IOS_FAMILY)
+#define HAVE_REMAP_JIT 1
+#endif
+
 #if PLATFORM(MAC)
 #define HAVE_SEC_KEYCHAIN 1
 #endif
